BT /F1 12 Tf 40 750 Td 14 TL (Photosynthesis and Cellular Respiration) Tj T* (Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose. It occurs in the chloroplasts, using chlorophyll to capture sunlight.) Tj T* (The overall reaction combines carbon dioxide and water to produce glucose and oxygen, releasing oxygen as a byproduct into the atmosphere.) Tj T* (Cellular respiration is the reverse process: mitochondria break down glucose using oxygen to release usable chemical energy in the form of ATP, releasing carbon dioxide and water as byproducts.) Tj T* (Together, photosynthesis and cellular respiration form a cycle that sustains most life on Earth by cycling carbon, oxygen, and energy between plants and animals.) Tj T* (Key vocabulary: chlorophyll, chloroplast, mitochondria, ATP, glucose, carbon cycle.) Tj ET
